Source offer (AGPL-3.0 Section 13)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GaussMeridian is a network-facing gateway. Section 13 of the GNU AGPL requires
that anyone who interacts with a running instance of this program remotely
through a computer network be offered the Corresponding Source of that instance,
free of charge, through a network server.

The Corresponding Source for unmodified GaussMeridian is:

  https://github.com/Gaussian-id/gaussmeridian

A running instance publishes this offer in two places, so a network user never
has to be told where to look:

  - The gateway advertises it in the `source` object returned by `GET /` and in
    the `x-source-offer` header on every HTTP response it serves.
  - The WebUI links it from the footer of every page.

If you deploy a MODIFIED version of GaussMeridian and let anyone reach it over a
network, that offer is yours to satisfy, not ours. You must publish your own
Corresponding Source — your modifications included — and point the two
mechanisms above at it. `SOURCE_OFFER_URL` (gateway) and
`NEXT_PUBLIC_SOURCE_OFFER_URL` (WebUI) exist for exactly that: set both to a URL
serving your build's source before you expose a modified instance to users.

